          "quote": "a) MSL expressly warrants that all Products, MSL supplied materials and Parts, and work prepared for IBM will conform in all material respects to the specifications, drawings, or other descriptions furnished or adopted by IBM, and will be of specified quality, good workmanship, and free from defect subject to the following terms:",
          "rationale": "MSL gives a real express warranty in our favour: SOW § 19.1 warrants conformance in all material respects to IBM specifications plus specified quality, good workmanship and freedom from defect, with stated periods for MSL Procured Parts (19.1(a)(iv)) and workmanship (19.1(a)(v)), running from delivery, surviving acceptance testing and expressly covering latent defects (19.1(b)). The remedy set matches the playbook: § 19.5 requires failure analysis, repair or replacement within the stated turnaround at MSL's expense and, if repair or replacement is not possible, a refund of MSL's price for the failed Product and Parts; § 19.7 adds epidemic-failure recall cost coverage, which exceeds the preferred position. The § 19.6 disclaimer is confined to implied and other terms relating to quality, merchantability, conformance and fitness and expressly preserves \"MSL'S WARRANTY OBLIGATIONS DESCRIBED IN THIS SECTION 19\", so it does not swallow the express warranty; there is no \"AS IS\" language. Two points noted but not flagged: (i) the durations in 19.1(a)(iv)-(v) are redacted ([*] months), so we should confirm on execution that they are at least 12 months for Products/Parts, and (ii) § 16.19 sunsets all representations and warranties on the [*] anniversary of the Effective Date, which we should confirm does not cut short Product warranties on units delivered late in the term. This is a manufacturing/Products deal, so the absence of a separate professional-and-workmanlike services warranty, compliance-with-laws warranty and malicious-code warranty is immaterial here, and the warranty exclusions in 19.1(a)(ii)-(iii) relate to IBM Parts and consigned Products (our own materials) and 19.3 to misuse, both customary. The clause benefits us, so no redline.",
